Subject: [PATCH] Fix Boost 1.90 compatibility

Boost 1.90 makes Boost.System fully header-only: conda-forge no longer
ships a compiled boost_system library or its CMake config
(boost_system-config.cmake). Two changes are needed for the build to find
Boost:

1. CMP0167 is forced to NEW so find_package(Boost) uses Boost's own
   BoostConfig.cmake instead of CMake's legacy FindBoost module. The legacy
   module carries a hardcoded dependency table that injects `system` as a
   dependency of thread/filesystem/chrono, which then fails because the
   boost_system config no longer exists. BoostConfig.cmake has no such
   reference and still provides the Boost_INCLUDE_DIRS / Boost_LIBRARIES
   compatibility variables this project relies on.

2. `system` is removed from the explicitly requested components, since it is
   header-only and has no config to find. Its headers remain available
   through Boost_INCLUDE_DIRS.
---
diff --git a/cmake/CMakeLists.txt b/cmake/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/cmake/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/cmake/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
     cmake_policy(SET CMP0144 NEW) # find_package() uses upper-case <PACKAGENAME>_ROOT variables.
 endif()
 if(POLICY CMP0167) # 3.30
-    cmake_policy(SET CMP0167 OLD)
+    cmake_policy(SET CMP0167 NEW)
 endif()
 
 project(IfcOpenShell VERSION ${RELEASE_VERSION})
@@ -310,7 +310,6 @@
     # @todo review this, shouldn't this be all possible header-only now?
     # ... or rewritten using C++17 features?
     set(BOOST_COMPONENTS
-        system
         program_options
         regex
         thread
